    {
      "id": "gin-2632",
      "scenario": "feature",
      "language": "Go",
      "pr_url": "https://github.com/gin-gonic/gin/pull/2632",
      "title": "feat(engine): add trustedproxies and remoteIP",
      "status": "completed",
      "duration_ms": 0,
      "references": [
        {
          "file": "context_test.go",
          "line": 1433,
          "body": "If we trust proxy `40.40.40.40`, but not trust `30.30.30.30` (proxy it is or not), then ClientIP should be `30.30.30.30` as `20.20.20.20` was set by somebody untrusted. Please do not forget that `X-Forwarded-For` is appended, so it should be processed right-to-left: right-most IP address is the IP address of the most recent proxy and the left-most IP address is the IP address of the originating client.",
          "cid": 694639407,
          "author": "agmt",
          "dimension": "correctness",
          "kind": "defect"
        },
        {
          "file": "context.go",
          "line": 756,
          "body": "Do you expect that HTTP proxy running on `c.RemoteIP()` resets `X-Forwarded-For`? Because if it appends, then we can't inherit trustiness of `c.RemoteIP()` to all other proxies.",
          "cid": 694643333,
          "author": "agmt",
          "dimension": "design",
          "kind": "design"
        }
      ],
      "findings": [
        {
          "file": "context.go",
          "line": 770,
          "severity": "high",
          "confidence": "high",
          "body": "RemoteIP 在每次请求中都调用 prepareTrustedCIDRs 并把结果写回引擎共享字段 c.engine.trustedCIDRs。Engine 被所有并发请求共享，且 Run 启动时也写入该字段，因此多个 goroutine 会对同一 slice header 并发写（写后再读），构成数据竞争；同时每个请求重复解析 CIDR 也带来无谓开销。",
          "evidence": "trustedCIDRs, _ := c.engine.prepareTrustedCIDRs()\n\tc.engine.trustedCIDRs = trustedCIDRs\n\tif c.engine.trustedCIDRs != nil {",
          "trigger": "用 gin.Default()/New() 启动服务后，任意并发请求调用 c.ClientIP() 或 c.RemoteIP()（默认 Logger 中间件或业务代码即可触发），在 go test -race / -race 运行时会报 DATA RACE。",
          "impact": "并发读写 slice header 可能读到撕裂值（指针与长度不匹配），导致 for 循环越界 panic 或使用到错误的 CIDR 列表，使服务在并发下不稳定。",
          "suggestion": "移除 RemoteIP 内的写回，改为在 Run（或 sync.Once/New 之后）一次性计算并缓存 engine.trustedCIDRs，请求路径只读；再用 go test -race 并发调用 ClientIP 验证无竞争。",
          "verification_status": "second_pass_review_passed",
          "verification_reason": "新增的 RemoteIP 在每次请求中执行 c.engine.trustedCIDRs = trustedCIDRs（context.go:771），而 c.engine 指向被所有请求 goroutine 共享的同一个 *Engine（context.go:56，Engine 作为 http.Handler 处理所有并发请求），Engine.trustedCIDRs 是普通 slice header 字段（gin.go:135），没有任何同步。同时 Run 也会写该字段（gin.go:333），且同一函数紧随其后读取它（context.go:772-773）。因此并发请求（默认 Logger/业务调用 ClientIP→RemoteIP）会对同一 slice header 非同步读写，构成 Go 内存模型下的数据竞争，-race 会报 DATA RACE，理论上可能读到指针与长度不匹配的撕裂值。触发路径明确、无需额外未核实前提。",
          "trace_id": "5fbe9e2976095ec4"
        },
        {
          "file": "gin.go",
          "line": 162,
          "severity": "medium",
          "confidence": "high",
          "body": "默认 TrustedProxies 只有 \"0.0.0.0/0\"，它是 IPv4 网络（4 字节掩码）。当 RemoteAddr 为 IPv6 时，IPNet.Contains 会因 IP 长度与网段长度不符返回 false，trusted=false，ClientIP 直接返回 IPv6 远端地址而忽略 X-Forwarded-For。旧实现不区分地址族，总是优先使用 X-Forwarded-For，故默认行为对 IPv6 场景发生改变。",
          "evidence": "TrustedProxies:         []string{\"0.0.0.0/0\"},",
          "trigger": "使用默认配置（未修改 TrustedProxies），服务监听 IPv6 或经 IPv6 代理转发，且请求头携带 X-Forwarded-For/X-Real-IP。",
          "impact": "ClientIP 退化为代理的 IPv6 地址而非真实客户端 IP，与旧行为不一致；基于 ClientIP 的限流、审计日志、ACL 会失效或误判。",
          "suggestion": "默认值补上 IPv6 网段，如 []string{\"0.0.0.0/0\", \"::/0\"}，并新增 RemoteAddr 为 IPv6 的用例断言 X-Forwarded-For 被采用；核实部署是否确会使用 IPv6。",
          "verification_status": "second_pass_review_passed",
          "verification_reason": "代码路径已完整查证：默认 TrustedProxies=[]string{\"0.0.0.0/0\"} 经 prepareTrustedCIDRs 解析为 IPv4 网络（net.ParseCIDR 得到 4 字节掩码）。Context.RemoteIP 使用 net.ParseIP 解析 RemoteAddr 后用 cidr.Contains(remoteIP) 判断；对真实 IPv6 地址（如 2001:db8::1），net.IPNet.Contains 中 ip.To4() 返回 nil，IP 长度 16 与网段长度 4 不符即返回 false，故 trusted=false。ClientIP 在 trusted=false 时直接返回 remoteIP.String()，完全跳过 RemoteIPHeaders（X-Forwarded-For/X-Real-IP）。因此在默认配置且远端为 IPv6 代理的请求中，X-Forwarded-For 被忽略、返回代理 IPv6 地址，导致限流/审计/ACL 依据错误地址。核心缺陷不依赖未展示的旧实现，仅由当前固定源码即可推导。",
          "trace_id": "001c5acce3e8ce42"
        }
      ],
      "reference_verdicts": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "verdict": "not_covered",
          "reason": "The reference comment is a defect about ClientIP's trust-walking algorithm: X-Forwarded-For is appended, so it must be parsed right-to-left and the test expectation at context_test.go:1433 (returning 20.20.20.20 when only 40.40.40.40 is trusted) is wrong. No system finding discusses X-Forwarded-For ordering, the ClientIP algorithm, or the test expectation — finding 0 is about a concurrency/performance issue in RemoteIP, finding 1 is about IPv6 defaults."
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "verdict": "not_covered",
          "reason": "The reference comment is a design question on RemoteIP (context.go:756): whether a proxy on RemoteIP() resets or appends X-Forwarded-For, i.e. whether trust of RemoteIP can be inherited by upstream proxies. Neither system finding addresses this — finding 0 is about the shared trustedCIDRs field/data race, finding 1 about IPv6 and the default TrustedProxies mask."
        }
      ],
      "finding_verdicts": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "verdict": "valid_new_issue",
          "reason": "Genuine, actionable concern anchored to the new code at context.go:770-771: RemoteIP recomputes prepareTrustedCIDRs on every request and assigns the result back to the engine-wide field, which the engine also writes at startup and which is shared across concurrent requests — a real data race plus redundant per-request CIDR parsing. The human reviewers did not raise this."
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "verdict": "valid_new_issue",
          "reason": "Anchored to the new default at gin.go:162. '0.0.0.0/0' is an IPv4 CIDR, so net.IPNet.Contains returns false for IPv6 addresses, making trusted=false and changing the previous behavior where X-Forwarded-For was always honored. This is a real, checkable behavior change the human reviewers did not comment on."
        }
      ],
