    {
      "id": "tokio-6001",
      "scenario": "performance",
      "language": "Rust",
      "pr_url": "https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/pull/6001",
      "title": "reduce the lock contention in task spawn.",
      "status": "completed_with_warnings",
      "duration_ms": 0,
      "references": [
        {
          "file": "tokio/src/runtime/task/list.rs",
          "line": 119,
          "body": "Having correctness rely on such things makes it very easy to introduce bugs when changing things. (The check for `closed` must happen while the shard mutex is locked; otherwise a task spawned during shutdown can be pushed to `OwnedTasks` but not removed by `close_and_shutdown_all`.)",
          "cid": 1368527199,
          "author": "Darksonn",
          "dimension": "correctness",
          "kind": "defect"
        },
        {
          "file": "tokio/src/runtime/task/list.rs",
          "line": 44,
          "body": "I don't really understand what the word \"grain\" means in this context. Can we add a doc comment explaining this, rename the field to something that better describes what it is, or both?",
          "cid": 1332175404,
          "author": "hawkw",
          "dimension": "readability",
          "kind": "suggestion"
        },
        {
          "file": "tokio/src/runtime/task/list.rs",
          "line": 78,
          "body": "it looks like `OwnedTasks::new` is only ever called with the values 1 and 16. What do you think about making this constructor private, and having the `pub(crate)` constructors be `new_current_thread` and `new_multi_thread` or something? that way, the value (which feels like an internal implementation detail) isn't leaked to the places where the `OwnedTasks` is constructed, and we can change the value in one place, rather than having to update _every_ call to `OwnedTasks::new`?",
          "cid": 1332181300,
          "author": "hawkw",
          "dimension": "design",
          "kind": "design"
        },
        {
          "file": "tokio/src/util/sharded_list.rs",
          "line": 32,
          "body": "```suggestion\n    unsafe fn get_shard_id(target: NonNull\u003cSelf::Target\u003e) -\u003e usize;\n```",
          "cid": 1382579513,
          "author": "Darksonn",
          "dimension": "maintainability",
          "kind": "suggestion"
        }
      ],
      "findings": [],
      "reference_verdicts": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "verdict": "uncovered",
          "reason": "The system produced no findings at all, so this concern about the `closed` check needing to happen while holding the shard lock is not addressed anywhere."
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
