    {
      "id": "redis-14017",
      "scenario": "performance",
      "language": "C",
      "pr_url": "https://github.com/redis/redis/pull/14017",
      "title": "Improve multithreaded performance with memory prefetching",
      "status": "completed",
      "duration_ms": 0,
      "references": [
        {
          "file": "src/config.c",
          "line": 3171,
          "body": "i personally think this is far too low level to be made a user config (and p.s. i don't see it in redis.conf). maybe we can completely drop it, and if not, let's make it a HIDDEN one.",
          "cid": 2106124779,
          "author": "oranagra",
          "dimension": "design",
          "kind": "design"
        },
        {
          "file": "src/db.c",
          "line": 374,
          "body": "if we do that, maybe we can cache the result so it can serve others usages (ACL, Cluster, ROF). besides, maybe instead of just computing the slot of the first key, it can already check for cross slot, and then the main thread won't have to. we did that in lookahead.",
          "cid": 2106125576,
          "author": "oranagra",
          "dimension": "design",
          "kind": "design"
        },
        {
          "file": "src/memory_prefetch.c",
          "line": 338,
          "body": "Function comment mentions that goal is to bring data to L1. Then, here it says I/O thread already did the look up but on a multi core machine (most machines nowadays), iothread and main thread will be on different cores and not sharing L1. I wonder if this comment is accurate or am I missing something. Maybe this was done for a very specific CPU.",
          "cid": 2112771801,
          "author": "tezc",
          "dimension": "correctness",
          "kind": "suggestion"
        },
        {
          "file": "src/memory_prefetch.c",
          "line": 394,
          "body": "If I'm not mistaken, we can do `batch-\u003ekeys_dicts[batch-\u003ekey_count] = kvstoreGetDict(c-\u003edb-\u003ekeys, (c-\u003eslot \u003e 0 ? c-\u003eslot : 0));` and delete `batch-\u003eslots`.",
          "cid": 2112804186,
          "author": "tezc",
          "dimension": "performance",
          "kind": "suggestion"
        },
        {
          "file": "src/memory_prefetch.c",
          "line": 231,
          "body": "Small kv objects of type string their values is embedded in the kv (i.e. `OBJ_ENCODING_EMBSTR`). In that case, maybe we can optimize and skip the step of `PREFETCH_VALDATA`.",
          "cid": 2097420269,
          "author": "moticless",
          "dimension": "performance",
          "kind": "suggestion"
        }
      ],
      "findings": [],
      "reference_verdicts": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "verdict": "uncovered",
          "reason": "No system findings were produced, so this design comment about dropping or hiding the prefetch-batch-max-size config was not addressed."
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "verdict": "uncovered",
          "reason": "No system findings were produced; the suggestion to cache the slot result and detect cross-slot in getSlotFromCommand was not raised."
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "verdict": "uncovered",
          "reason": "No system findings were produced; the concern about IO thread vs main thread not sharing L1 cache was not raised."
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "verdict": "uncovered",
          "reason": "No system findings were produced; the simplification of batch-\u003ekeys_dicts and removal of batch-\u003eslots was not raised."
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "verdict": "uncovered",
          "reason": "No system findings were produced; the optimization to skip PREFETCH_VALDATA for OBJ_ENCODING_EMBSTR strings was not raised."
        }
      ],
